					}

					Informational: {
						MealSizeScanner: {
							/* Short:
								'''
								Shows the size of nearby snacks, and helps you know if you're able to make them your next meals
								Functions from the inventory as well as normal accessory slots
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								''' */
							/* Long:
								'''
								Most things that you can eat [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:display their size as a meal below themselves].
								If their size number is [c/00FF00:green], you are able to swallow them with ease.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target meal would fit in your stomach normally, and nothing is keeping you from gobbling them up on sight. Go indulge a little!]
								If their size number is [c/FFFF00:yellow], you are able to swallow them, but might have a bit of trouble keeping them down or properly mulching them.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that while your target meal would fit in your stomach normally, one of the following is true:]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your stomach is too full to fit them due to other meals already inside it]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's defense exceeds your stomach's digestion tick damage]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's health exceeds 1 minute of your stomach's final DDPS (digestion damage per second, factors in defense)]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your target meal's acid resist level exceeds your stomach's acid tier]
								If their size number is [c/FF0000:red], you aren't able to gulp and gurgle them into gut fat yet.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target meal wouldn't fit in you due to your throat and/or stomach capacity being too low.]
								[c/7F7F7F:If this is the case, try to increase your GLP and TUM stats by whatever means you find throughout the game!]
								Functions from the inventory as well as when equipped in normal accessory slots.
								''' */
							/* Flavor:
								'''
								This peculiar device was originally designed for use by a mechanic to ensure optimal fullness-to-caloric-value weighting when consuming nearby living creatures and converting them into (potential) energy.
								It can do the same for you, if you care to, though its main use will almost certainly be making sure your eyes don't get bigger than your stomach...and/or throat.
								''' */
						}

						PredCapacityScanner: {
							/* Short:
								'''
								Shows the stomach capacity of nearby entities that can eat you, and lets you know if you're able to take some time off in their gut
								Functions from the inventory as well as normal accessory slots
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								''' */
							/* Long:
								'''
								Most things that can eat you [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:display their stomach capacity as predators above themselves].
								If their capacity number is [c/00FF00:green], they're able to swallow you with ease.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that your choice predator could fit you in their stomach normally, and nothing is keeping them from gobbling you up on sight. Ready to get gurgled?]
								If their capacity number is [c/FFFF00:yellow], they're able to swallow you, but might have a bit of trouble keeping you down or properly mulching you.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that while your target pred could fit you in their stomach normally, one of the following is true:]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Their stomach is too full to fit you due to other meals already inside it]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your defense exceeds their digestion tick damage]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your health exceeds 20 seconds of their stomach's final DDPS (digestion damage per second, factors in defense)]
								[c/7F7F7F:> Your acid resist level exceeds your desired predator's stomach's acid tier]
								If their capacity number is [c/FF0000:red], they aren't able to gulp and gurgle you into gut fat.
								[c/7F7F7F:This means that your target predator isn't able to eat you, since their stomach won't be able to hold you. A sad day, indeed.]
								Functions from the inventory as well as when equipped in normal accessory slots.
								''' */
							/* Flavor:
								'''
								Exposing an electronics implement to shimmer, most times, doesn't actually short-circuit it like water or stomach acid might, but instead tends to warp the implement's functionality to a new use case similar to, yet also very different, its initial purpose.
								This almost otherworldy-looking device performs a similar task to its non-shimmered counterpart, but analyzes the digestive capacity of scanned subjects instead. While this is useful for anyone looking to get mulched by a nice, hungry tummy, it's not particularly useful to a predator in comparison to its normal form.
								''' */
						}
					}

					Vanity: {
						BalloonBelly: {
							/* Short:
								'''
								Can be blown up or deflated, and wrapped around your tummy to make it look bigger!
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								''' */
							/* Long:
								'''
								Can be worn in any vanity accessory slot to make your stomach always appear larger proportional to the size of the balloon.
								Current size is {InflatedSize}; maximum size is {MaximumInflatedSize}.
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Left-click] to inflate the balloon if it is not at its max size, increasing its size by 1.
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Right-click] to deflate the balloon if it has air in it, decreasing its size by 1.
								Does nothing when equipped in a non-vanity accessory slot.
								''' */
							// Flavor: This funny-looking balloon is pre-fitted with a waistband for easy attachment to...well, specifically the stomach. Blow it up enough, and it'll replicate all the great looks of a massive, meat-filled gut without any of the downsides, complete with color-changing latex exterior so you get just the matching color you and your tummy want! Just note that it won't make all the happy gurgling and groaning a REAL bellyful of squirmy snacks makes.
						}
					}

					AntiDigestionSash: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Decreases taken digestion damage and slows Softened buildup slightly
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases taken digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{AntiDigestionSashDigestionDefenseBonus}].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Slows Softened buildup] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{AntiDigestionSashSoftenedBuildupReduction}].
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							A simple sash made out of leathers, feathers, and silk, often hastily put together and worn by less confident adventurers.
							While it won't hold up to a continued gastric assault, it can help stave off the acids of a hungry tummy in a pinch.
							''' */
					}

					NymphHairScarf: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Increases movement speed and lowers stomach weight
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases movement speed] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{NymphScarfMoveSpeedBuff}].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{NymphScarfWeightReduction}].
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							A pleasantly comfortable scarf sewn with the luscious locks of at least one or two delicious, deceitful damsels found throughout Terraria's great caverns.
							Sewn into the scarf are sapphires and miniature runes which allow the wearer to be lighter on their feet, even (or perhaps, especially) with a good gutful of meat (still alive or otherwise) slowing them down, mimicking the stomach-centric swiftness of a hungry nymph.
							''' */
					}

					PromethiaAntiDigestionSash: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Decreases taken digestion damage and slows Softened buildup substantially
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases taken digestion damage] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PromethiaAntiDigestionSashDigestionDefenseBonus}].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Slows Softened buildup] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PromethiaAntiDigestionSashSoftenedBuildupReduction}].
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							A sparkly, tasty-looking sash made of a material similar to gold, yet possessing the consistency of silk...as well as some actual divine-looking silk, this sash is standard-issue equipment for lower-ranking Sinhunters from the heavens beyond.
							It holds up against greedier gastric assaults much better than its mortally-designed counterpart, and is designed to grant eaten angels some time to properly teach their predator just how low said predator still is on the greater food chain.
							St. Promethia, of course, keeps hers with her not because she wants to get out of the predators that snack on her, but rather, because she wants just a little more time to...enjoy herself, for lack of a better term, inside those hungry tummies.
							''' */
					}

					ShroomNecklace: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Increases your max number of minions by 1
							Strengthens your fungal fairies
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Increases your maximum number of minions] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:1].
							Confers the following buffs to fungal fairies you own summoned by the [i:V2/ShroomStaff] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Fungal Fairy Staff]:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Halved] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:movement speed penalty] from weight gain.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:1.35x] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:food absorption rate].
							- Fungal spores grant [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:'Fungal Blessing'] for [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:4] seconds each [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:(or ][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:12 seconds][c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}: if eaten)].
							''' */
						// Flavor: A blue necklace, fitted with a mysterious mushroom that seems to leave a positive impact on fungal fairies.
					}
				}

				Charms: {
					BetterDigestion: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Makes your acids a little bit stronger
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						// Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases ACI] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{AcidStrengthBonus}]."
						// Flavor: A beginner-level charm designed to make the bearer's stomach acids substantially more potent than if they were to go without it. Very useful for first-time predators who could really use that extra kick to their digestive juices to secure their first few big meals, though sadly not particularly worthwhile past those starting stages.
					}

					Fatass: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Lets you take on much bigger prey...but at what cost?
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Doubles] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:swallow and stomach capacities].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Halves] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:digestion damage and tick rate].
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							A high-risk, high-reward charm typically only offered to skilled adventurers with a greedy enough tummy to negate its downside; it is often plucked from these adventurers by nymphs as one of the few things that can survive the gastric torment of such deceitful ladies' gluttonous tummies.
							While worn, it redirects a part of the muscle and nerve firings from actively digesting swallowed prey, instead putting that bodily power towards stretching the throat and stomach to gobble up and gorge oneself on ever-larger prey. It's not hard to see why nymphs see them as a valuable trinket, as would anyone else.
							''' */
					}

					LessStomachWeight: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Makes your stomach lighter, but only if you're not too full
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Decreases stomach weight] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{WeightReduction}].
							If your stomach is at {FullnessEffectivenessLossThreshold} fullness or more, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:this effect becomes less effective the less capacity you have to spare.]
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							A rather strange charm, almost mechanical in nature, purpose-built to make one's stomach significantly less of a burden to lug around while it's filled to capacity with sufficiently satisfying caloric fuel.
							While it works in most cases, it does this by passively generating a layer of helium inside of the bearer's stomach; thus, if there isn't sufficient room to provide said helium deposits, the charm becomes significantly less effective, to the point of eventually doing nothing if there is no space to add helium.
							''' */
					}

					PreyItemTheft: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							May cause you to belch up certain items from your meals
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Upon dying to digestion,] prey you eat [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:have a chance to drop certain items].
							Some items dropped this way will be [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:unique] to these tables, while others will be [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:existing drops] from the prey (with [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:lower/limited drop rates]).
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							A very simple charm.
							The only noteworthy thing about it is the big, shiny...tasty coin...perfectly...in the center...

							...donning it makes you feel incredibly...hungry. Hungry for valuables. Maybe your future meals would be kind enough to give you some so you don't end up snacking on your tasty new charm?
							''' */
					}

					RegenFromAbsorption: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Grants health and mana regeneration while digesting dead prey
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							While digesting dead prey, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:based on how much you absorb in a minute:]
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Increases health regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{HealthRegenerationRatio} of absorption rate in HP/sec]. [c/7F7F7F:(Natural)]
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:Increases mana regeneration] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{ManaRegenerationRatio} of absorption rate in MP/sec].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Effectiveness decreases if there are prey in your stomach still alive.]

							Current regeneration ({RegenEffectiveness} effectiveness with {LivePreyRemaining} out of {PreyRemaining} prey still alive):
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:{CurrentHealthRegen} HP/sec]
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.ManaHeal}:{CurrentManaRegen} mana/sec]
							''' */
						// Flavor: An intermediate-level charm designed to ease the long-standing issue of one's digestive system granting surprisingly little reprieve from the heat of battle. As long as a surplus of food resides in the bearer's stomach, this charm will convert some of the excess calories into mana to fuel a spell which revitalizes the bearer both physically and magically. Of course, this spell can only work as quickly as the bearer's belly can digest its meals.
					}
				}

				Consumables: {
					Catchables: {
						Pinky: {
							/* Short:
								'''
								When used, a delicious little Pinky is released into the world
								Hold the Swallow key while using this item to instantly gulp down the released Pinky
								Has a very pleasantly sweet taste, granting a few buffs when eaten
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								''' */
							/* Long:
								'''
								When eaten by anything:
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.Heal}:Heals for {PinkyEatHeal} health] instantly upon running out of health.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Happy! buff] while in a stomach; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{PinkyEatHappyLength} seconds] once fully digested.
								- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Regeneration buff] while digesting; this lingers for [c/FFFF00:{PinkyEatRegenLength} seconds] once fully digested.
								May have any number of positive consequences if given to someone as a sweet treat of a gift.
								''' */
							/* Flavor:
								'''
								With how diverse slimes are in size, shape, and savor, it's no surprise that some slimes end up hunted almost exclusively for their beloved flavor. No slime embodies this more directly than the Pinky, a very small slime which is HIGHLY prized for the following traits:
								1) Its bite-size nature, allowing even the smallest and most inexperienced of predators to swallow it with relative ease.
								2) Its lovely flavor, which much resembles cotton candy, though almost all are uncertain as to where this sweet flavoring actually originated.
								3) Its vibrant pink coloration, from which it gets its name.
								''' */
						}
					}

					PermanentUpgrades: {
						PureSwallowBoost1: {
							/* Short:
								'''
								Permanently increases the strength of your throat when used or eaten
								Can only be used once; further uses and/or consumptions do nothing special
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								''' */
							/* Long:
								'''
								[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Using or eating this item] will permanently grant you the following bonus:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases GLP] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{PureSwallow1GLPBonus}].
								This bonus only applies once. Using or eating this item after you have already done so [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:will have no further effect].
								''' */
							/* Flavor:
								'''
								One of the first physical stimulants for predators ever created was a drug to enhance the potential of the throat, allowing for easier swallowing of anything, and anyone, that the recipient wanted packed into their gut.
								This stimulant has been replicated countless times, and is now standard-fare as an entry-level predatory aid across the world of Terraria.
								''' */
						}
					}

					Potions: {
						FastDigestionPotion: {
							/* Short:
								'''
								Speeds up digestion while digesting
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								''' */
							/* Long:
								'''
								Induces a variety of predatorily-centric effects when drank, almost all involving digestive power.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 1 minute thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+{FastDigestionPotionACIBonus} ACI]
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+{FastDigestionPotionABSBonus} ABS]
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Raises acid tier to 3][c/7F7F7F:, if it is not at 3 already]
								''' */
							/* Flavor:
								'''
								Digestive aids are commonplace in medical establishments across Terraria to help with particularly rowdy or troublesome prey, with just about every option that entails available for use to make sure your system doesn't get backed up with all the parts of your prey you can't quite melt down (yet).
								This is a rather simple variant carried by medical practitioners at all times (be they for your use or theirs). Dropping something small into the bottle seems to cause it to be swiftly dissolved by the mysterious substance within...not that it's much of a surprise, really. Even inanimate objects can be ravenously hungry --- enough to eat a person, in the right circumstance. People just always seem to make great meals...

								...well, that snack in your stomach won't wait much longer. Bon appetit!
								''' */
						}

						StomachCapacityPotion: {
							/* Short:
								'''
								Allows your stomach to hold a bit more than usual while digesting
								'For when you're craving an extra snack or two for dessert'
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								''' */
							/* Long:
								'''
								Improves your stomach's holding capacity when drank.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+{StomachCapacityPotionCapacityBonus} stomach capacity]
								''' */
							/* Flavor:
								'''
								A commonplace and easily-brewable predatory enhancer in the Terrarian world, this potion uses a simple mix of relaxing agents, mainly found in fish, to allow a predator's stomach to stretch a good bit past its normal limits.
								Sadly, though, it won't bolster your stomach's durability against internal fighting at all; you'd best hope you can keep down all that extra meat you'll be able to fit into your hungry tummy.
								''' */
						}

						StomachacheMeterCapacityPotion: {
							/* Short:
								'''
								Improves your stomach's resistance to the struggles of your prey while digesting
								{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
								''' */
							/* Long:
								'''
								Improves your stomach's ability to keep prey from causing a ruckus inside you when drank.
								Since you're just swallowing the whole potion, bottle and all, you'll need the bottle to break first from running out of durability.
								You're awfully lucky that glass is really easy to digest, and low in calories to boot.

								Once the bottle breaks, until fully digested, and for 3 minutes thereafter:
								> [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Increases stomachache meter capacity] by [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionMeterCapacityBonus}].
								> The struggles of your prey will deal [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:-{StomachacheMeterCapacityPotionUneaseDefenseBonus} less struggle damage].
								''' */
							/* Flavor:
								'''
								One of a number of common brews made for predatory types, this potion is often sold by medical practitioners to those who need that one particularly feisty femme or burly breakfast they had to settle down and digest, ideally without hacking them back up.
								It makes use of several well-known gastric relaxants to ease the stomach and throat, lowering the amount that unruly prey can kick up a stomachache and heightening the amount they'd need to do so in order to induce vomiting.
								''' */
						}
					}

					SpecialItemUpgrades: {
						PaperMaidSummon: {
							RawStats: {
								/* Short:
									'''
									{PaperMaidName} might like this item
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									''' */
								/* Long:
									'''
									This item can be fed to {PaperMaidName}, the paper maid summoned by the [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{$Mods.V2.ItemName.Voraria.Weapons.Summon.PaperMaidSummon}], by right-clicking on her with it.
									Once she fully digests this item, {PaperMaidName} will permanently gain automagic self-lamination, conferring to her the following buffs:
									> +{LaminatedHealth} health.
									> +{LaminatedStomachCapacity} stomach capacity.
									> +{LaminatedStomachacheMeterCapacity} stomachache meter capacity.
									> +{LaminatedDigestionRatio} digestion damage ratio.
									''' */
								/* Flavor:
									'''
									This small device, a marvel of magical conduction cross-bred with machine lamination, is designed to be able to laminate anything and everything simply by placing the desired item inside it and waiting.
									Early prototypes proved incapable of accepting people as input and laminating. These prototypes have since been stored in their creator's personal stash for later dismantling.
									That said, while lamination is often used as a tool to hunt origami creations in the wild, fallen off trading caravans and originally left over from Sveetia's annual Sugar Crane Festival, it is also used by the Sveetian people to reinforce their greatest works.
									''' */
							}

							Flight: {
								/* Short:
									'''
									{PaperMaidName} might like this item
									{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
									''' */
								/* Long:
									'''
									This item can be fed to {PaperMaidName}, the paper maid summoned by the [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{$Mods.V2.ItemName.Voraria.Weapons.Summon.PaperMaidSummon}], by right-clicking on her with it.
									Once she fully digests this item, {PaperMaidName} will permanently gain paper crane wings, conferring the following buffs:
									> Gains flight capabilities, and will fly as her master or target does.
									> Increased accuracy and range for dash attack ([c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:RIGHT-RIGHT-RIGHT] instruction).
									''' */
								/* Flavor:
									'''
									A poor, damaged origami crane, worn down by evading the ever-growing hunger of the average office worker for a nice, well-laminated snack from Sveetia while on lunch break.
									While its wings are battered and its flight rendered all but gone, it still has strength to give...but not to those who would hunt it for a light meal.
									No, this weak, dying crane searches for another of its kin, another Sveetian origami piece, to give itself wholly to...

									...lending, to that creation, the great power of flight.
									''' */
							}
						}
					}

					DigestionRepairScroll: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Using this item will instantly relieve you of most of the downsides of predator or preything lifestyles
							After it is used, a full day must pass before it can be used again
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							This item can only be used once at least one full day has passed since the last time it was used.
							Upon usage, it will instantly:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Fully repair all items in your inventory] that have taken digestion damage and can be repaired.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Remove all Softened stacks still applied to you] from any lingering acid burns from recent encounters.
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Clear all indigestion-related debuffs you may have] from particularly troublesome meals.
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							It's a scroll, inscribed with countless runes that you've never seen before; notably, they look surprisingly similar to, yet so very different from, musical notes...which would help, if the scroll bothered to say anything about the actual composition of the piece. Whoever wrote this sheet music didn't think it through very well from the perspective of one who might want to play it.
							In any event, incomprehensible as it may be at a cursory glance, as you go to look at it closer, the runes fade into the background somewhat, and a second layer of text fades in which is actually comprehensible to the average person:

							[c/FF3FBF:CHORUS (sing in D# major):]
							[c/FF3FBF:From heavens inward and a cauldron outward, the Conductress' graces shall smile.]
							[c/FF3FBF:By Melodia's song, this verse, when not wrong, shall save from a fate all too vile.]

							[c/FF3FBF:I near face the Veil, the edge of our great hail, as a chance predator's left me weak,]
							[c/FF3FBF:So by Melodia's song, I sing a chorus along, for my strength to return to its peak.]

							[c/7F1F5F:POST-CHORUS (composer's note):]
							[c/7F1F5F:But the song must rest, asleep in its nest, 'fore its strength can remend its own peak,]
							[c/7F1F5F:So by my sacred song, don't dare sing this wrong; I've no care for the melodically weak.]

							...you can't help but wonder if Promethia stole this from someone.
							''' */
					}

					DigestionUpgradeTablets: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Can only be eaten once you've fully gained the stomach-strengthening effects of Life Fruit and enchanted your stomach acids beforehand
							Permanently modifies your digestive system using a delayed-effect bioalteration spell once fully digested
							This mixes nitric acid into the structure of your stomach acid, turning it into aqua regia (royal water)
							This change makes your stomach significantly better at digesting things, and allows you to digest more things you wouldn't normally be able to
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							This item can only be eaten once you have eaten and digested at least {LifeCrystalsMax} Life Crystals, at least {ManaCrystalsMax} Mana Crystals, and at least {LifeFruitMax} Life Fruits.
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently grants +40 ACI.]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Permanently grants +20 ABS.]
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:Raises your acid tier to Royal (2).]
							This upgrade is permanent, but only takes effect once the pack is fully digested.
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							Despite how often these things were flaunted around as the future of predatory prowess and a marvel of modern magical bioengineering back in the day, the real marvel is that these somehow pose no significant health risks despite mixing an entire secondary acid into an already-powerful stomach. The label on the side suggests eating the entire pack...including the pack itself. The pack supposedly has much better nutritional value than the pills, so...bottoms up.
							Obtaining more than one pack of these tablets is prohibited by Avarsician law and punishable by...well, predominantly fucking about and learning what for. It's not exactly hard to guess why a spell that assumes you haven't taken the pills at all is bad if you've already melted down a full pack of them before.
							''' */
					}

					FeatherDuster: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Can only be used in a hungry tummy
							Can be used to tickle and/or agitate your predator's stomach a lot; often enough for them to belch you back up
							'Now taken very literally'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							Can only be used while inside something's stomach.
							When used, instantly [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:deals] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{FeatherDusterStruggleDamage}] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:struggle damage] to your predator.
							If this would fill up their stomachache meter, it instead caps at its usual maximum, and you are [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:instantly belched out].
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							Often carried around by the bundle by harpies, the core purpose of this feathery broom-like implement is to agitate the stomach of hungry predators, forcing them to belch and/or cough up whatever (and WHOever) they ate alongside the user.
							More modern uses for evolved forms of this implement include maids' cleaning work, on-the-job snacks for said maids, impromptu microphones-turned-mini-meals on budget karaoke nights, and mitigating a wide array of magical incantations.
							''' */
					}

					HairDyeCapacity: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Changes the color of your hair based on how full you are
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Changes the color of your hair] based on [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:how full your stomach currently is].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:When your stomach is empty], makes your hair a dark red.
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:When your stomach is completely full], makes your hair a pleasantly full green.
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							A special hair dye, purpose-mixed for the fashionable predator in your life (be it yourself or someone else).
							On a full stomach, this dye gives off a stunningly pleasant green, while the dark red one's hair will turn while running on empty is just as attractive. A number of other colors end up in the spotlight if the wearer's stomach isn't 100% full, but still has some meat in it, and all of them are specially designed to make one's hair as appealing as possible.
							After all, how can your prey resist ending up a part of those luscious locks if you've got just the right color to make them weak in the knees?

							DISCLAIMER: Excess calories from digested meals may not actually increase hair length.
							''' */
					}

					SteampunkerGutFastTravel: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Can only be used in a hungry tummy?
							Can be used to save yourself from impending digestion into ass fat, probably?
							'The latest and greatest in instantaneous transportation!...or so she says.'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							Can only be used while the Steampunker is alive.
							When used, instantly [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:teleports you] [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:out of your current predator's stomach], if applicable...[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:and into the Steampunker's].
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:Does not work] while in the Steampunker's stomach.
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							A peculiar little trinket fashioned together by the Steampunker, the great lass she is, for a measly sum.
							It can be used anywhere as a one-way teleport, even workable in the most gluttonous guts to instantly get you out of digestive jeopardy...but to what catch?
							Much to the Steampunker's frustration, though, it doesn't yet work across planes of reality, nor from excessively long distances. She's still working on that functionality.
							''' */
					}

					DemonCandy: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Provides regeneration when digested
							'Isn't this just a jawbreaker covered in chocolate?'
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							When eaten:
							- [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Grants the Regeneration buff] after running out of durability; this lingers for [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:{Regen} minutes].
							If dropped onto the ground in the Underworld, it might bait out certain types of monsters.
							''' */
						/* Flavor:
							'''
							It is, infact, a jawbreaker covered in chocolate.
							Appears to be the favourite food of a certain type of monster in the lava-filled depths of the Underworld.
							''' */
					}

					GhostBall: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							If a certain ghost isn't present, throwing this into a surface will summon them
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						// Long: "[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:Summons Echo], who behaves similar to a Town Pet. You will be able to have them live in a house with another Town NPC."
						// Flavor: Not quite a spirit bomb, but you can pretend it is, i guess.
					}
				}

				TransformationItems: {
					BaelzTransformationItem: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Transforms you into a chaotic rat girl while in the inventory
							You may be susceptible to weight gain under the effect
							Right click to toggle effect
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							While active:
							By default, you have [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:+10%] critical chance, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:+15%] attack speed,
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:+30%] movement speed, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:-35%] damage, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:-15%] damage reduction,
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:-20%] stomach capacity & [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+25%] absorption rate
							Critical chance increases when gaining weight.
							On a critical hit, the chance is rolled again, dealing a double crit that [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:doubles damage] if successful.
							Additionally, prey in your stomach can take critical damage, using the critical chance given by this item.
							''' */
						// Flavor: tba
					}

					KroniiTransformationItem: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Transforms you into a (seemingly) elegant lady while in the inventory
							You may be susceptible to weight gain under the effect
							Right click to toggle effect
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							While active:
							By default, you have +10% movement speed, +20% jump height, -25% damage reduction,
							+33% body weight reduction, -1 flat body weight & -15% stomach weight reduction.
							Melee attacks add 1.25 seconds of [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:Time Acceleration], which increases melee attack speed, acid & absorption effectiveness.
							Time Acceleration can stack up to [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:30 seconds].
							Melee attacks additionally have a [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:10% chance to freeze an enemy in time] for [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:2 seconds].
							This chance is affected by luck.
							After the enemy is unfrozen, they cannot be frozen again for a second, or 5 seconds if it's a boss.
							''' */
						// Flavor: tba
					}

					OllieTransformationItem: {
						/* Short:
							'''
							Transforms you into a crazy zombie girl while in the inventory
							You may be susceptible to weight gain under the effect
							Right click to toggle effect
							{$Mods.V2.ItemTooltip.Generic.HoldForInDepthFunctionAndLore}
							''' */
						/* Long:
							'''
							While active:
							By default, you have [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:+20%] movement speed, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+45%] stomach capacity, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:-1] flat stomach weight,
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:+67%] stomach weight reduction, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:-67%] acid damage, [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeVoreEffect}:-67%] absorption rate & [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.NegativeEffect}:-10%] ranged damage.
							Non-homing ranged attacks deal more damage the further away the target is, up to [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:1.75x damage].
							You can [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:dash toward your cursor] by pressing [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.DoSomething}:(Ollie: Dash)], dodging enemies and projectiles while granting
							a [c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveEffect}:drastically increased firing rate] for a short time.
							[c/{$Mods.V2.CommonColorCodes.PositiveVoreEffect}:You may also end up 'accidentally' swallowing things you dash into...]
							''' */
						// Flavor: tba
					}

					SoraTransformationItem: {
